<title>SWITZERLAND: SBC lowers rate on some cash bonds.</title>
<headline>SBC lowers rate on some cash bonds.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss Bank Corp (SBC) said it was lowering the interest rate it pays on some of its cash bonds (Kassenobligationen) with effect from Monday, September 9.</p>
<p>SBC gave the following details:</p>
<p> Cash bonds		  New Rate		Old Rate</p>
<p> Two years		   2.5 percent	   2.5 percent</p>
<p> Three years		 3.0 percent	   3.25 percent</p>
<p> Four years		  3.25 percent	  3.50 percent</p>
<p> Five years		  3.5 percent	   3.75 percent</p>
<p> Six years		   3.75 percent	  4.0 percent</p>
<p> Seven years		 4.0 percent	   4.0 percent</p>
<p> Eight years		 4.25 percent	  4.25 percent</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
